Commit 0b97665 ("Say what a gpu => 1 die may already have changed on the host", Refs k25) corrects a previously wrong claim in Rex::Rancher.pm POD ("GPU hardware support"): it no longer claims a gpu_setup die happens before ANY host change. It now says at most pciutils has been installed for detection, or - for index-dependent sources on e.g. Ubuntu - the package index has already been refreshed and repositories added/enabled before the die.

This is exactly the kind of option-semantics correction an operator doing incident triage after a failed gpu => 1 deploy would rely on, and it is not covered by the existing "{{$NEXT}}" bullet about GPU hardware support (which only covers driver-generation selection, vGPU guest die and the NVLink warning - see 551f109, bf69987, 01f85f7).

Add a short bullet to Changes under {{$NEXT}}, or fold a clause into the existing GPU hardware support bullet, naming the corrected die-timing claim.

